Thanks for the advice, people - however I have noticed most people posted
this and didn't email it as requested. In fact I got only 1 answer from
anyone in a timely fashion, and that was my friend who also plays on
nyx - apparently he read it. Anyhoo. I decided to go on without assistance.
ID'd rings blindly by putting them on until I found the levitation ring
(try #2 =), and from then on it was child's play. Found the statues. Kicked
the door in. Voila...Ms. M. ID'd her as the real thing via '/'...and she
was in *clear visual angle* of me...and I of her (obviously, or I could
not have seen her...)...and I did *NOT* turn to stone. Not even close.
Had no reflection, etc etc etc. Nothing except my good looks and a lev.
ring. Oh...and, er, the ToM. =) Dug around in my bag of holding, took
a quick shower, wrapped a towel around my head (ahem =): You detect a
well known spoiler, read it?), and proceeded to make sushi of her. Unwrapped
and went on, after debating "Gee. Should I eat the corpse, or will it
pull a cockatrice on me?"

Died 3 levels later...in the Land of the Dead. (Lev. rings are really handy
in the castle just above the Land...for obvious reasons...)...Hacked n
slashed left n right, no problem...then figured "Eh...I haven't prayed
for a while. I think ol' Ameratasu owes me (with my 2 blessed luckstones)".
Prayed.

Moloch was *none* too happy. (Maybe I shold have worn the amulet that was
un ID'd in my bag.) How was I to know, though? (chuckle) 600K pts,
a decent game...and I learned quite a bit.

Question *only* for those who Know: If you wish for your Quest item,
(like I blunderingly did - but I didn't regret it =)...and you stash
it in a bag before you bump into the Guardian of your Quest...
will the program let you go downstairs anyways? Or will you still get
"A mysterious force prevents you from entering..." (digging, of course,
did not work either.)...I blundered and the 2nd time I bumped into the
Guardian, I just hapened to be toting around my Quest item in visible
view...and he treated it as if I had solved the Quest. So, dev team or
other experts, please assist. =) I mean, given the choice between finding
the ToM and wishing for it and then stashing it later...I'd *much* rather
wish for it. =) Heh.

